                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "brazilwoods"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67fdccfa-21fc-3a74-aba6-33be4d79836e",
                        "entry_id": "65b6bedf-0ce5-3bd3-9dc9-e6152cdf527b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Brazilian timber tree (Paubrasilia echinata, syn. Caesalpinia echinata), used primarily to make bows for string instruments."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c981ece6-8c32-3aa3-968f-6aee034a1a03",
                        "entry_id": "65b6bedf-0ce5-3bd3-9dc9-e6152cdf527b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The wood of this tree."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d912f74b-f00d-4ba4-addb-eed7bc93d4cb",
                                "sense_id": "c981ece6-8c32-3aa3-968f-6aee034a1a03",
                                "text": "He would take with him red brasilwood from the East Indies – a dye-wood that was so valued that when a few years later the Portuguese found it in the New World, they would name a country after it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "28949161-d0b1-460a-afed-a80b152b5ead",
                        "source_entry_id": "65b6bedf-0ce5-3bd3-9dc9-e6152cdf527b",
                        "source_sense_description": "timber tree",
                        "target_lang_word": "pernambouc",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pernambouc",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be27e916-c6c4-3bd6-948c-85236574da50",
                                        "entry_id": "517de09c-1b29-366a-bf69-8bba107aae37",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Bois de Pernambouc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62dea3d9-2e11-4795-b837-7591b6e35072",
                                                "sense_id": "be27e916-c6c4-3bd6-948c-85236574da50",
                                                "text": "D'autres bois peuvent être utilisés comme l’amourette (Brosimum guianense, Moraceae) pour les archers^([sic]) baroques, plus dense que celui du pernambouc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96cb6cac-e43e-4464-abb6-3c7d8ae29c56",
                                                "sense_id": "be27e916-c6c4-3bd6-948c-85236574da50",
                                                "text": "Pendant ce temps, les frères Verrazano qui n’avaient pas contourné le cap de Bonne-Espérance se dirigèrent vers l’ouest et touchèrent les côtes de l’Amérique du Sud, notamment celles du Brésil où ils embarquèrent des cargaisons de pernambouc, un bois rouge à partir duquel on préparait à l’époque des teintures."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
